Analysis includes: case of Transfer before Withdrawal completion 
What happens if Withdraw 1000 and Transfer 1000 are not in sync?
How is double spending prevented? 
- Collateral moves have precedence over DLT updates 
- DLT updates have precedence over retail transfers 

Consistency Hierarchy:
1. Collateral accounts (Flexcube)
2. DLT
3. Retail DBs accounts

=> Transfers are safe only if collateral accounts are updated first
===> Queued collateral moves (listener logic) may fail if a transfer makes it invalid after withdrawal

Deadlock? 
1. Withdrawal collateral move ok
1.1 DLT update start for withdrawal (...no two-phase commits with rollback of Flexcube here...)
2. Transfer initiated (nobody is blocking it)
2. DLT update for transfer ok (DLT wallets have still funds... 1.1 is not finished yet)
3. DLT update start for withdrawal FAILS (collateral accounts being wrong)



end note



